---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Contribute | OpenInterstate"
  description="Help build open US interstate highway data. Naming review, schema review, examples, and documentation are the most useful early contributions."
>
  <section>
    <h1>Contribute</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The highest-leverage contributions right now aren't code. Names,
      schemas, and release shapes harden quickly once people build on them,
      so the most valuable thing you can do is review them while they are
      still cheap to change. Worked examples and clearer docs are a close
      second.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Repos</h2>
    <ul class="links">
      <li><a href="https://github.com/tldev/openinterstate">github.com/tldev/openinterstate</a>: the main project</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/tldev/openinterstate-reachability">github.com/tldev/openinterstate-reachability</a>: drive-time reachability scores between interstate exits and nearby POIs</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/tldev/openinterstate.org">github.com/tldev/openinterstate.org</a>: this site</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Current focus</h2>
    <p>
      The pipeline and the schema contract are in place, and releases ship
      regularly. The work now is data quality: filling gaps in exit names and
      numbers, growing place coverage, and populating the exit_aliases table.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
